d comic aesthetic. The shadow terminator uses rotated UV coordinates with a specific frequency to create crisp pen crosshatching, which needs to be carefully color-coded to avoid muddy greys.\n\n\nThe scene's comic materials dynamically shift color palettes \n<truncated 324 bytes>\nviolet shadows, cool cyber-cyan highlights, and a Spider-2099 laser crimson/electric ultraviolet dual rim kick.\n\n\nThe scene's elements are now dynamically driven by the `scene[\"sv_dimension\"]` property. The `V5_SkyDome` transitions between three distinct Spider-Verse sky palettes based on this dimension value.  `LGT_V5Sun` and `LGT_V5SkyFill` also smoothly shift their color and energy corresponding to the active sky dimension. The goal is to achieve visual consistency across these changing elements.\n\n\nThe focus is on creating dynamic visual effects tied to animation triggers within the scene.  Comic ribbon strips, with a specific material and exposed properties, are parented to body and wing bones to create a trailing effect, controlled by animation parameters for scaling, rotation, and flutter. Wheel smear effects are also considered, which will be parented to relevant bones.\n\n\nFocusing on dynamic visual effects tied to animation triggers, particularly on the race car. Wheel smear arcs, using a specific material, are being created to generate the illusion of speed, synced with wheel movement.\n\nExhaust cone effects are being implemented, triggered by animation parameters, using a multi-layered material to create comic afterburner and upshift effects.\n\nFinally, graphic spark slash shards are being generated, also controlled by animation triggers and a specific material, designed to appear under the car's rear floor plank edges.\n\n\nFocusing on animating spark slash shards triggered by animation. Will tie these shards to car speed and proximity to kerbs, ensuring they appear when the car exceeds certain speed thresholds or nears specific track elements.\n\nRigorous testing is essential. A 26-shot raycast is planned to ensure no camera occlusions are introduced by the new visual effects across the entire animation. Precise bone parenting and transform calculations will be verified in Blender to guarantee accurate mesh placement, cross-checking the existing setup of the rear wing endplate and front tire for reference.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"& \\\"D:\\\\APPs\\\\steam\\\\steamapps\\\\common\\\\Blender\\\\blender.exe\\\" -b \\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\LATEST\\\\v5_stage_anim.blend\\\" --python-expr \\\"\\nimport bpy\\nfrom mathutils import Vector\\nsc = bpy.context.scene\\nsc.frame_set(1)\\ndeps = bpy.context.evaluated_depsgraph_get()\\nrig = bpy.data.objects['RIG_F1_Race'].evaluated_get(deps)\\nm_head = rig.matrix_world @ rig.pose.bones['Bone_Heading'].matrix\\ninv_head = m_head.inverted()\\nfor nm in ['GEO_F1_RearWing_Endplate_L', 'GEO_F1_FrontWing_Endplate_L', 'GEO_F1_Exhaust_TitaniumTail', 'GEO_F1_Tire_FL', 'GEO_F1_Tire_RL']:\\n    ob = bpy.data.objects[nm].evaluated_get(deps)\\n    pts = [inv_head @ (ob.matrix_world @ Vector(c)) for c in ob.bound_box]\\n    mn = tuple(round(min(p[i] for p in pts), 3) for i in range(3))\\n    mx = tuple(round(max(p[i] for p in pts), 3) for i in range(3))\\n    print(f'{nm:30s} in car-space: {mn} .. {mx}')\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolSummary":"\"Get exact car-space bounds of wing tips, exhaust, and tires\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
